window.EN={"1":"Adding the surviving retainers of the Kingdom of Leonster to the Fiana Freeblades and the Magi Squad,","2":"Leif's \"Liberation Army,\" having put together, after a fashion, the makeup of an army,","3":"in order to head at last to the relief of Tahra,","4":"was about to cross the border between the Empire and Thracia once more.","5":"It was a small ravine deep in the mountains that people call \"Noel Canyon\"...","6":"General Largo, is all well?","7":"Why, Lady Olwen. Out scouting again today?","8":"There's hardly going to be a battle this deep in the mountains. You work hard every day.","9":"The scouting duty is General Kempf's order. He assigns it only to Lady Olwen... I can only think it is harassment.","10":"Oh, Fred, I'd rather be outside than in Fort Dandrum.","11":"After all, I don't have to see that Kempf's face.","12":"Ho ho ho. My, what spirit you have.","13":"But General Kempf is a troublesome man, too.","14":"Born to the high nobility, with his future assured, and yet he is somehow small as a person.","15":"To envy General Reinhardt's fame and harass you, his sister... Truly, it is conduct shameful in a soldier.","16":"General Kempf is convinced that my brother is his rival.","17":"...They are close in age, and both became generals young. It is not that I can't understand the feeling, but...","18":"But my brother doesn't think of it that way at all...","19":"That, too, is probably something General Kempf does not like.","20":"? Why is that?","21":"!? You don't understand? ...No wonder, you are still young.","22":"? ?","23":"That aside, since you have come all this way, take your time and rest...","24":"Yes, thank you. Then I shall take you up on that...","25":"Lord Leif, this is Noel Canyon. What you see over there is the fort guarding the Empire's border.","26":"So at last we advance into imperial territory. What is the enemy's strength?","27":"The garrison is small, but they have long-range bows called long arches.","28":"Their power is tremendous, and unless we destroy them first, taking the fort is impossible.","29":"Then what do we do?","30":"There are three ways.","31":"Draw the enemy with the main force, and meanwhile take them out with a detached force. That is the middling plan.","32":"Use cavalry and pour in all at once. That is the poor plan.","33":"And the best plan, the important one?","34":"Having said this much, you surely understand already, Lord Leif.","35":"There should be no need for me to spell it out.","36":"Lady Olwen, someone has launched an attack.","37":"I will hold them here, so I would like you to convey this to Dandrum.","38":"If possible, I would like to help as well. Won't you permit me?","39":"No. Your duty is scouting. Reporting comes first.","40":"I am glad for the thought, but you had better return to Dandrum.","41":"Then at least, for as long as time allows...","42":"...If you insist that much.","43":"But only until the time you must return to Dandrum. Is that clear?","44":"Thank you. Fred, let's go!","45":"Yes!","46":"I have to get back to Dandrum soon...","47":"Sir Largo, I will return with reinforcements without fail. Please stay safe until then...","48":"General Largo... He was quite the warrior.","49":"That was my first time fighting the Friege army, but they fought splendidly.","50":"If that was a small frontline unit, I dread the battles ahead.","51":"Yes. House Friege is an illustrious house, so even its lowest soldiers value honor.","52":"Their discipline as an army is probably among the top one or two on the continent.","53":"For that reason they can be called a formidable foe, but your way of fighting was no less splendid than the enemy's, Prince.","54":"Are you talking about taking General Largo prisoner without killing him?","55":"Yes.","56":"To fight this holy war through with righteousness is to carry on the will of the late Prince Quan.","57":"From here on as well, I hope we will not lose our pride as knights and will always fight fair and square.","58":"Pride as knights... huh.","59":"You're right. Needless slaughter is the one thing I don't want to commit...","60":"August, did you see the enemy mage knight who withdrew in the middle of the battle?","61":"A female knight. She was quite a tough opponent.","62":"Who could she be?","63":"She went toward Fort Dandrum, so she probably went back to report on us.","64":"Which means the enemy is lying in wait for us.","65":"That is so. Fort Dandrum is, to begin with, a sturdy fortress said to be impregnable.","66":"On top of that, we have given the enemy the leeway to prepare a defense.","67":"If Dandrum's commander is an able general, we will be forced into a hard fight.","68":"But there's no other route, is there?","69":"Correct. To go to Tahra, there is no way but through Dandrum.","70":"Then we have no choice but to go. If we dawdle, we'll only be at a greater disadvantage!","71":"You who violate our territory, what on earth is your aim!","72":"Mmh... So this is the end...","73":"I need no mercy! Strike off my head!!","74":"This is imperial territory. Leave at once!","75":"You dare violate Friege's territory? Who are you people!","76":"Oh, aren't you the Liberation Army people?","77":"Do your best. Drive the invaders out of this Thracia for us.","78":"I know, take this staff with you. I'm sure it will come in handy.","79":"You're members of the Liberation Army, right? Hang in there. I'm rooting for you.","80":"I know, take this staff. It's sure to come in handy."};
